\begin{lemma}
\label{lemma-cech-Hausdorff-quasi-compact}
Let $X$ be a Hausdorff and quasi-compact topological space. Let
$\mathcal{F}$ be an abelian sheaf on $X$. Then
the map $\check{H}^n(X, \mathcal{F}) \to H^n(X, \mathcal{F})$ defined
in (\ref{equation-cech-to-cohomology}) is an isomorphism for all $n$.
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
Every open covering of $X$ has a finite subcover, which is a locally finite
refinement. Thus $X$ is paracompact and the result follows from
Lemma \ref{lemma-cech-paracompact}.
\end{proof}
